<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Status-bar silhouette of the Solid Share mark.

    Android draws a notification small icon from its ALPHA CHANNEL ONLY: every non-transparent
    pixel is repainted with the notification colour and the artwork's own colours are discarded.
    An icon whose parts are stacked opaque shapes therefore collapses into a featureless blob.

    The mark survives that because logo.xml draws it as a SINGLE path: the hexagon is filled and
    the molecule is a hole in it, wound the opposite way so the default nonZero fill leaves it
    transparent. Recolouring the fill white keeps the molecule as negative space, exactly as the
    monochrome launcher layer renders it.

    The viewport is square (logo.xml's is 486x434, which a square 24dp canvas would stretch), and
    the group centres the art in it: the mark spans x [18.0, 466.0] and y [16.1, 418.9], so it
    already fills ~92% of the width — the platform's live area — and needs only centring.
-->
